IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `nz-part2-principles`
IMPORT `nz-part2-definitions`
IMPORT `nz-part2-commencement-repeal`
IMPORT `nz-part2-revision-incorporation`
IMPORT `nz-part3-publication`
IMPORT `nz-part5-oversight`
IMPORT `nz-part6-7-pco-regulations`
IMPORT `nz-schedules`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under New Zealand legislation, or who needs to know when legislation takes effect or how it is to be read,
-- asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and
-- no layer-1 module was changed to suit it. Every question calls a layer-1 rule; the only things built here are the records and lists the rules take,
-- from the plain answers the person gives (yes or no, a number, a date, or one of the modules' own choices).
-- A person who is an official (a Minister, the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, the House) has no seat here: what the Act asks of them is encoded in layer 1,
-- and appears below only as what it means for the person (a deadline to meet, a right that survives, a document that proves something).
-- Where the text is silent, or the facts a question needs are outside the encoding, the answer is NOTHING (or a constructor that says the Act does not say),
-- never a guess. The calendar questions ask for the seven days the Act names but does not date, for the year the person is asking about; if the search for the
-- next working day crosses into a year the person did not give, the answer is NOTHING.

-- Builds the calendar the layer-1 rules take, from the seven dates the person states for the year. Nothing is decided here.
GIVEN `Waitangi Day falls on` IS A DATE
      `Good Friday falls on` IS A DATE
      `Easter Monday falls on` IS A DATE
      `Anzac Day falls on` IS A DATE
      `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` IS A DATE
      `Matariki Observance Day falls on` IS A DATE
      `Labour Day falls on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Named day`
`the calendar I state` `Waitangi Day falls on` `Good Friday falls on` `Easter Monday falls on` `Anzac Day falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` `Matariki Observance Day falls on` `Labour Day falls on` MEANS
    LIST (`Named day` OF `Waitangi Day`, `Waitangi Day falls on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `Good Friday`, `Good Friday falls on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `Easter Monday`, `Easter Monday falls on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `Anzac Day`, `Anzac Day falls on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `the Sovereign's birthday`, `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `Matariki Observance Day`, `Matariki Observance Day falls on`)
       , (`Named day` OF `Labour Day`, `Labour Day falls on`)

§ `Legislation Act 2019 -- the questions of a person with a period to count`

§§ `Reading and applying legislation (Part 1 and Part 2, ss 5 to 23)`

@export Is this instrument secondary legislation (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `it is made under an Act, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument made under an Act, directly or through other secondary legislation?
      `that Act or other legislation says it is secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that Act, or other legislation, say the instrument is secondary legislation?
      `it is made under the Royal prerogative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument made under the Royal prerogative?
      `its form and purpose are set out in Schedule 1A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its form and purpose set out in Schedule 1A of the Legislation Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this instrument secondary legislation` IS
    `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF `it is made under an Act, directly or indirectly`, `that Act or other legislation says it is secondary legislation`, `it is made under the Royal prerogative`, `its form and purpose are set out in Schedule 1A`)

@export Do the Legislation Act's rules of reading apply to the legislation I am reading (s 9)?
GIVEN `the legislation is part of the laws of New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the legislation you are reading part of the laws of New Zealand?
      `the legislation says the Act's rules do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation itself say that the Legislation Act's rules of reading do not apply to it?
      `the context requires a different reading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the legislation require it to be read differently from the Act's rules?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Act's rules of reading apply to the legislation I am reading` IS
    `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` `the legislation is part of the laws of New Zealand` `the legislation says the Act's rules do not apply` `the context requires a different reading`

@export Does the legislation govern what happened on my day (s 11)?
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the circumstance arise?
      `the day the legislation came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the legislation come into force?
      `the legislation has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the legislation been repealed?
      `the day it is repealed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is it repealed? (any date if it has not been repealed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the legislation govern what happened on my day` IS
    `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` `the day it happened` `the day the legislation came into force` `the repeal day I state`
    WHERE
        `the repeal day I state` MEANS IF `the legislation has been repealed` THEN JUST `the day it is repealed` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does the legislation apply to something that happened before it came into force (s 12)?
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the circumstance arise?
      `the day the legislation came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the legislation come into force?
      `the legislation says it applies to the past` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation itself say it applies to earlier circumstances?
GIVETH A `Application to a past circumstance`
DECIDE `Does the legislation apply to something that happened before it came into force` IS
    `whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` `the day it happened` `when it came into force on` `the day the legislation came into force` `and it provides otherwise` `the legislation says it applies to the past`

@export Is this day a working day (s 13)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `Waitangi Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Waitangi Day fall this year? (6 February, unless it is moved)
      `Good Friday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Good Friday fall this year?
      `Easter Monday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Easter Monday fall this year?
      `Anzac Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Anzac Day fall this year? (25 April)
      `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Sovereign's birthday observed this year?
      `Matariki Observance Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Te Ra Aro ki a Matariki / Matariki Observance Day fall this year?
      `Labour Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Labour Day fall this year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day a working day` IS
    `is a working day` `the day I am asking about` `according to` `my calendar`
    WHERE
        `my calendar` MEANS `the calendar I state` `Waitangi Day falls on` `Good Friday falls on` `Easter Monday falls on` `Anzac Day falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` `Matariki Observance Day falls on` `Labour Day falls on`

@export Does my notice count as public notification (s 13)?
GIVEN `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice published in the Gazette?
      `it is published in a newspaper circulating in the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it published in one or more newspapers circulating in the area the matter relates to or arises in?
      `it is on an Internet site run by or for the person who must publish it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it published on an Internet site run by or on behalf of the person who must or may publish it?
      `the site is publicly available as far as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that site publicly available, as far as practicable?
      `the site is free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that site free of charge?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my notice count as public notification` IS
    `is public notification` (`Publication of a notice` OF `it is published in the Gazette`, `it is published in a newspaper circulating in the area`, `it is on an Internet site run by or for the person who must publish it`, `the site is publicly available as far as practicable`, `the site is free of charge`)

@export Is what I have prepared writing under the Act (s 13)?
GIVEN `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it represent or reproduce words, figures or symbols?
      `the form and medium of the words` IS A `Form and medium of words` @desc In what form and medium are the words, figures or symbols: in print, written or typed on paper, fixed on a physical object, shown only on a screen, or spoken only (not visible)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I have prepared writing under the Act` IS
    `is writing` `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` `the form and medium of the words`

@export Does the Act define the word I am relying on (s 13)?
GIVEN `the word` IS A `Word for a stretch of time` @desc Which word are you relying on: day, week, month, year, working day or sitting day?
GIVETH A `What the Act says of a word`
DECIDE `Does the Act define the word I am relying on` IS
    `what the Act says of` `the word`

@export Are my partner and I in a de facto relationship under the Act (s 14)?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `my partner's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your partner, in years?
      `we live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union?
      `we are married to, or in a civil union with, each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or in a civil union with, each other?
      `anyone aged 16 or 17 has the consent the Care of Children Act 2004 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If either of you is 16 or 17, has that person obtained consent under section 46A of the Care of Children Act 2004? (say yes if neither is)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my partner and I in a de facto relationship under the Act` IS
    `is a de facto relationship` (`Relationship between two people` OF `my age in years`, `my partner's age in years`, `we live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union`, `we are married to, or in a civil union with, each other`, `anyone aged 16 or 17 has the consent the Care of Children Act 2004 requires`)

@export Is my posted document taken to have been sent (s 17)?
GIVEN `the legislation authorises or requires the document to be sent by post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation authorise or require the document to be sent by post (serve, give or send)?
      `the document is properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document properly addressed?
      `the document is prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the postage prepaid?
      `the document was posted as a postal article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you post it as a postal article?
      `someone has proved the document was not sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone proved that the document was not sent?
      `someone has proved the document was not received then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone proved that the document was not received at the time it would ordinarily be delivered?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it be delivered in the ordinary course of post?
GIVETH A `Whether sending is taken as done`
DECIDE `Is my posted document taken to have been sent` IS
    `whether the document is taken to be sent` (`Posting facts` OF `the legislation authorises or requires the document to be sent by post`, `the document is properly addressed`, `the document is prepaid`, `the document was posted as a postal article`, `someone has proved the document was not sent`, `someone has proved the document was not received then`, `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`)

@export On what day is my posted document taken to have been received (s 17)?
GIVEN `the legislation authorises or requires the document to be sent by post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation authorise or require the document to be sent by post (serve, give or send)?
      `the document is properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document properly addressed?
      `the document is prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the postage prepaid?
      `the document was posted as a postal article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you post it as a postal article?
      `someone has proved the document was not sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone proved that the document was not sent?
      `someone has proved the document was not received then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone proved that the document was not received at the time it would ordinarily be delivered?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it be delivered in the ordinary course of post?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my posted document taken to have been received` IS
    `the day the document is taken to be received` (`Posting facts` OF `the legislation authorises or requires the document to be sent by post`, `the document is properly addressed`, `the document is prepaid`, `the document was posted as a postal article`, `someone has proved the document was not sent`, `someone has proved the document was not received then`, `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`)

@export Is the Crown bound by this Act or part of an Act (s 22)?
GIVEN `legislation expressly says the Crown is bound by the Act or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act, or other legislation, expressly say the Crown is bound by this Act or this part of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Crown bound by this Act or part of an Act` IS
    `an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown` `legislation expressly says the Crown is bound by the Act or part`

@export Does an example in the legislation limit the provision it illustrates (s 23, Schedule 1 clause 4)?
GIVEN `the day the legislation was enacted or made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the legislation containing the example enacted or made?
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE @desc What is the main commencement date of the Legislation Act 2019? (the day section 10 of the Legislation (Repeals and Amendments) Act 2019 came into force)
      `the example is in a later amendment to that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the example in an amendment made after the main commencement date to that older legislation?
      `the legislation says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation itself say section 23 does not apply, or apply?
      `the context requires a different reading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the legislation require it to be read differently?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an example in the legislation limit the provision it illustrates` IS
    IF `section 23 applies to the example in legislation enacted or made on` `the day the legislation was enacted or made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date` `where it is in a later amendment:` `the example is in a later amendment to that legislation` `and the legislation provides otherwise:` `the legislation says otherwise` `or the context requires:` `the context requires a different reading` THEN `an example limits the provision` TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `When legislation takes effect, and when it stops (ss 25 to 39)`

@export On what day does the Act, or my part of it, come into force (s 25)?
GIVEN `the kind of provision` IS A `Kind of provision` @desc Is it an ordinary provision, the Title, a commencement section, or a principal legislation provision?
      `the Act states or provides a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act state or provide for a date on which the Act or part comes into force?
      `the date the Act states or provides` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (any date if there is none)
      `the day of Royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Act receive Royal assent?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the Act or my part of it come into force` IS
    `the day on which an Act or a part of an Act comes into force` `the kind of provision` `with the date stated` `the date stated` `and Royal assent on` `the day of Royal assent`
    WHERE
        `the date stated` MEANS IF `the Act states or provides a date` THEN JUST `the date the Act states or provides` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does a reference in the commencement section reach the provision I am looking at (s 25)?
GIVEN `the kind of provision` IS A `Kind of provision` @desc Is the provision an ordinary provision, the Title, a commencement section, or a principal legislation provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a reference in the commencement section reach the provision I am looking at` IS
    `a reference in the commencement section of an Act includes` `the kind of provision`

@export On what day does the secondary legislation, or my part of it, come into force (s 26)?
GIVEN `the kind of provision` IS A `Kind of provision` @desc Is it an ordinary provision, the Title, a commencement provision, or a provision identifying the principal legislation amended?
      `it states or provides a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the secondary legislation state or provide for a date on which it comes into force?
      `the date it states or provides` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (any date if there is none)
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the secondary legislation made?
      `it has been published or made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been published or first made available yet?
      `the day it was first published or made available` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it first published or made available? (any date if not yet)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the secondary legislation or my part of it come into force` IS
    `the day on which secondary legislation or a part of it comes into force` `the kind of provision` `with the date stated` `the date stated` `made on` `the day it was made` `and first published or made available on` `the day it was published`
    WHERE
        `the date stated` MEANS IF `it states or provides a date` THEN JUST `the date it states or provides` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day it was published` MEANS IF `it has been published or made available` THEN JUST `the day it was first published or made available` ELSE NOTHING

@export At what moment does the legislation come into force (s 27)?
GIVEN `the day the legislation names` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the legislation say it comes into force (or from)?
      `it says it comes into force from that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say it comes into force 'from' that day, rather than 'on' it?
      `it states a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state a particular time of day?
      `the hour it states` IS A NUMBER @desc What hour does it state (0 to 23)? (0 if none)
      `the minute it states` IS A NUMBER @desc What minute does it state (0 to 59)? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE Moment
DECIDE `At what moment does the legislation come into force` IS
    `the moment at which legislation comes into force` `the day the legislation names` `it says it comes into force from that day` `it states a particular time` `the hour it states` `the minute it states`

@export On what day does the legislation come into force if it says a number of months after my event (s 28)?
GIVEN `the number of months` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many months does the legislation say it comes into force?
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event occur (for example, Royal assent)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the legislation come into force a number of months after my event` IS
    `the day of commencement` `the number of months` `months after` `the day of the event`

@export On what day does the legislation come into force if it says a number of days, weeks, months or years after my event (s 28)?
GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many units does the legislation say it comes into force?
      `the unit` IS A `Unit of time` @desc Is the number counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event occur (for example, Royal assent)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the legislation come into force a number of units after my event` IS
    `the day of commencement when expressed as` (`Period length` OF `the number`, `the unit`) `after` `the day of the event`

@export Do my existing rights, and a proceeding I am in, survive the repeal or amendment (s 33)?
GIVEN `the matter or thing relates to my existing legal position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter or thing you want to complete relate to a right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status or capacity you already had?
      `the proceeding I want to start relates to my existing legal position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proceeding you want to start relate to such an existing position?
      `my proceeding was started or in progress under the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proceeding started, or in progress, under the legislation before it was repealed or amended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my existing rights and proceedings survive the repeal or amendment` IS
    `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` `the matter or thing relates to my existing legal position` `the proceeding I want to start relates to my existing legal position` `my proceeding was started or in progress under the legislation`

@export Am I still liable for an offence I committed before the law was repealed or amended (s 34)?
GIVEN `the day I committed the offence or breach` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence or breach committed?
      `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the repeal or amendment take effect?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still liable for an offence I committed before the law was repealed or amended` IS
    `the liability for an offence or breach committed on` `the day I committed the offence or breach` `is unaffected by a repeal or amendment taking effect on` `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`

@export May the old law still be used to deal with my offence (s 34(2))?
GIVEN `what the old law would be used for` IS A `Purpose for which repealed legislation continues` @desc Would the old law be used for investigating the offence, for starting or finishing a proceeding, or for imposing a penalty or other order?
      `the day I committed the offence or breach` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence or breach committed?
      `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the repeal or amendment take effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the old law still be used to deal with my offence` IS
    `repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` `what the old law would be used for` `for an offence or breach committed on` `the day I committed the offence or breach` `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`

@export What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today (s 37)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the new legislation is to replace or correspond to existing legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new legislation to replace, or to correspond to, existing legislation?
      `the new legislation has a commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a day been set for the new legislation to come into force?
      `the day the new legislation comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day does it come into force? (any date if none is set)
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a reference to new legislation is a reference to`
DECIDE `What does a reference to new legislation that is not yet in force refer to today` IS
    `what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` `the day I am asking about` `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` `the new legislation is to replace or correspond to existing legislation` `and comes into force` `the commencement I state`
    WHERE
        `the commencement I state` MEANS IF `the new legislation has a commencement date` THEN JUST `the day the new legislation comes into force` ELSE NOTHING

@export What does a reference in legislation to repealed legislation mean now (s 38)?
GIVEN `there is legislation that replaces or corresponds to the repealed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there legislation that, with or without modification, replaces or corresponds to the repealed legislation?
GIVETH A `What happens on repeal to a reference to the repealed legislation`
DECIDE `What does a reference in legislation to repealed legislation mean now` IS
    `what a reference in legislation to repealed legislation is` `there is legislation that replaces or corresponds to the repealed legislation`

@export Is legislation that is repealed from a certain day still in force on my day (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day the legislation is to be repealed from` IS A DATE @desc From what day is the legislation expressed to be repealed?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is legislation repealed from a certain day still in force on my day` IS
    `legislation expressed to be repealed from` `the day the legislation is to be repealed from` `is still in force on` `the day I am asking about`

@export Is legislation that is repealed on a certain day still in force on my day (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day the legislation is to be repealed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the legislation expressed to be repealed?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is legislation repealed on a certain day still in force on my day` IS
    `legislation expressed to be repealed on` `the day the legislation is to be repealed` `is still in force on` `the day I am asking about`

@export Does legislation that is to remain in force until a certain day still apply on my day (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day it remains in force until` IS A DATE @desc Until what day is the legislation expressed to remain in force or have effect?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does legislation that remains in force until a certain day still apply on my day` IS
    `legislation expressed to remain in force until` `the day it remains in force until` `is still in force on` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Counting a period of time (ss 54 to 58)`

@export On which day does my period end (ss 54 and 56)?
GIVEN `how many` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units long is the period?
      `the unit` IS A `Unit of time` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how the period is introduced` IS A `How a period is introduced` @desc Does the legislation say the period starts on or begins on a day, or runs from or after a day or event (or within so many days of it)?
      `the day or the day of the event` IS A DATE @desc What is that day, or the day of that event?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end` IS
    `the last day of a described period` (`Period length` OF `how many`, `the unit`) `that is` `how the period is introduced` `by reference to` `the day or the day of the event`

@export On which day does my period end if the legislation names the closing day (s 54)?
GIVEN `how the period is closed` IS A `How a period is closed` @desc Does the legislation say the period ends on a day, continues until a day, or ends before the start of a day?
      `the day named` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the legislation name?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end if the legislation names the closing day` IS
    `the last day of a period that is` `how the period is closed` `by reference to` `the day named`

@export On which day may I first do the second thing if at least so many working days must lie between (s 54 Item 7)?
GIVEN `the working days required between` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days must lie between the two events (counting neither event's day)?
      `the day of the first event` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the first event?
      `Waitangi Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Waitangi Day fall this year? (6 February, unless it is moved)
      `Good Friday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Good Friday fall this year?
      `Easter Monday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Easter Monday fall this year?
      `Anzac Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Anzac Day fall this year? (25 April)
      `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Sovereign's birthday observed this year?
      `Matariki Observance Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Te Ra Aro ki a Matariki / Matariki Observance Day fall this year?
      `Labour Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Labour Day fall this year?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day may I first do the second thing if working days must lie between` IS
    `the earliest day for the second event if at least` `the working days required between` `working days must lie between it and the first event on` `the day of the first event` `according to` `my calendar`
    WHERE
        `my calendar` MEANS `the calendar I state` `Waitangi Day falls on` `Good Friday falls on` `Easter Monday falls on` `Anzac Day falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` `Matariki Observance Day falls on` `Labour Day falls on`

@export Until which day may I do the thing if my last day is not a working day (s 55)?
GIVEN `the day or the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc What is the day, or the last day of the period, on which the thing must or may be done?
      `Waitangi Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Waitangi Day fall this year? (6 February, unless it is moved)
      `Good Friday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Good Friday fall this year?
      `Easter Monday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Easter Monday fall this year?
      `Anzac Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Anzac Day fall this year? (25 April)
      `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Sovereign's birthday observed this year?
      `Matariki Observance Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Te Ra Aro ki a Matariki / Matariki Observance Day fall this year?
      `Labour Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Labour Day fall this year?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which day may I do the thing if my last day is not a working day` IS
    `the last day on which the thing may be done under section 55` `the day or the last day of my period` `according to` `my calendar`
    WHERE
        `my calendar` MEANS `the calendar I state` `Waitangi Day falls on` `Good Friday falls on` `Easter Monday falls on` `Anzac Day falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` `Matariki Observance Day falls on` `Labour Day falls on`

@export Am I in time if I do the thing on this day (s 55)?
GIVEN `the day or the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc What is the day, or the last day of the period, on which the thing must or may be done?
      `the day I do the thing` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you do it?
      `Waitangi Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Waitangi Day fall this year? (6 February, unless it is moved)
      `Good Friday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Good Friday fall this year?
      `Easter Monday falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Easter Monday fall this year?
      `Anzac Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Anzac Day fall this year? (25 April)
      `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the Sovereign's birthday observed this year?
      `Matariki Observance Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Te Ra Aro ki a Matariki / Matariki Observance Day fall this year?
      `Labour Day falls on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does Labour Day fall this year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time if I do the thing on this day` IS
    `the thing due by` `the day or the last day of my period` `may be done on` `the day I do the thing` `according to` `my calendar`
    WHERE
        `my calendar` MEANS `the calendar I state` `Waitangi Day falls on` `Good Friday falls on` `Easter Monday falls on` `Anzac Day falls on` `the Sovereign's birthday is observed on` `Matariki Observance Day falls on` `Labour Day falls on`

@export At what New Zealand time does my moment fall (s 57)?
GIVEN `the UTC day` IS A DATE @desc On what date (in UTC) is the moment?
      `the minutes after midnight UTC` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes after midnight UTC is it?
      `the offset that the Time Act 1974 fixes` IS A NUMBER @desc What offset from UTC, in minutes, does the Time Act 1974 fix for New Zealand then? (720 for standard time, 780 for daylight time)
GIVETH A Moment
DECIDE `At what New Zealand time does my moment fall` IS
    `the New Zealand time of` `the UTC day` `at` `the minutes after midnight UTC` `with offset` `the offset that the Time Act 1974 fixes`

@export Is my distance within the limit, measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane (s 58)?
GIVEN `the first place's metres east` IS A NUMBER @desc How many metres east of your reference point is the first place?
      `the first place's metres north` IS A NUMBER @desc How many metres north is the first place?
      `the second place's metres east` IS A NUMBER @desc How many metres east is the second place?
      `the second place's metres north` IS A NUMBER @desc How many metres north is the second place?
      `the limit in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the distance limit, in metres?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my distance within the limit measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` IS
    `the distance between` `the first place` `and` `the second place` `is no more than` `the limit in metres` `metres`
    WHERE
        `the first place` MEANS Place OF `the first place's metres east`, `the first place's metres north`, 0  -- placeholder: the height is never read (section 58 ignores height)
        `the second place` MEANS Place OF `the second place's metres east`, `the second place's metres north`, 0  -- placeholder: the height is never read

§§ `Material that secondary legislation incorporates by reference (ss 64 to 66, Schedule 2)`

@export Do the later changes to the material my regulation incorporates have legal effect (s 66)?
GIVEN `the material was incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the material incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64?
      `the originator amended the material after the secondary legislation was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the originator of the material amend it after the secondary legislation was made?
      `the changes were specifically incorporated by later legislation made under Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the changes specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2?
      `another Act expressly authorises the changes to have that effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act expressly authorise the changes to have that effect?
GIVETH A `Effect of an amendment to incorporated material`
DECIDE `Do the later changes to the incorporated material have legal effect` IS
    `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` `the material was incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` `the originator amended the material after the secondary legislation was made` `the changes were specifically incorporated by later legislation made under Schedule 2` `another Act expressly authorises the changes to have that effect`

@export Is the chief executive's certified copy enough to prove the material that was incorporated (Schedule 2 clause 4)?
GIVEN `a copy certified by the chief executive is produced in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy certified as correct by the chief executive of the administering agency produced in the proceeding?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that the copy is not correct?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the certified copy enough to prove the incorporated material` IS
    `the certified copy is sufficient evidence of the material incorporated` `a copy certified by the chief executive is produced in the proceeding` `there is evidence to the contrary`

§§ `Publication and official versions (ss 69 to 81)`

@export Am I entitled to read the legislation free of charge on the legislation website (s 72)?
GIVEN `it is legislation published by the PCO under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Parliamentary Counsel Office published the legislation under the Legislation Act?
      `access is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is access to it practicable at the moment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to read the legislation free of charge on the legislation website` IS
    `a person may access or download the legislation from the legislation website free of charge` `it is legislation published by the PCO under this Act` `access is practicable`

@export What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove (s 79)?
GIVEN `the kind of official version` IS A `Kind of official version` @desc Is it as originally enacted or made, a consolidation, a version with editorial changes, or a consolidation with editorial changes?
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has anyone shown the official version to be wrong?
GIVETH A `What an official version is taken to prove`
DECIDE `What is the official version of the legislation taken to prove` IS
    `what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` `the kind of official version` `unless the contrary is shown:` `the contrary is shown`

@export Must the court take judicial notice of the legislation, so that I need not prove it (s 81)?
GIVEN `it is a court or a person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision-maker a court or a person acting judicially?
      `it is legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you are relying on legislation (an Act, or secondary legislation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court take judicial notice of the legislation` IS
    `must take judicial notice` `it is a court or a person acting judicially` `of` `it is legislation`

§§ `Parliament's oversight of secondary legislation (ss 114 to 127)`

@export Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time (s 117)?
GIVEN `a Committee member gave notice of a motion to disallow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a member of the Committee responsible for reviewing secondary legislation give notice of a motion to disallow it?
      `the deadline` IS A DATE @desc What is the deadline (the close of the 21st sitting day after the notice was given)?
      `the notice was withdrawn by the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice withdrawn on or before the deadline?
      `the House disposed of the motion by the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the House dispose of the motion on or before the deadline?
      `Parliament was dissolved or expired by the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was Parliament dissolved, or did it expire, on or before the deadline?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the secondary legislation I rely on disallowed because the House did not deal with the motion in time` IS
    `the secondary legislation is disallowed under section 117` `a Committee member gave notice of a motion to disallow it` `the deadline` `the withdrawal I state` `the disposal I state` `the dissolution I state`
    WHERE
        `the withdrawal I state` MEANS IF `the notice was withdrawn by the deadline` THEN JUST `the deadline` ELSE NOTHING
        `the disposal I state` MEANS IF `the House disposed of the motion by the deadline` THEN JUST `the deadline` ELSE NOTHING
        `the dissolution I state` MEANS IF `Parliament was dissolved or expired by the deadline` THEN JUST `the deadline` ELSE NOTHING

@export On what day does the House's amendment of the secondary legislation I rely on take effect (s 119)?
GIVEN `the day a copy of the resolution was published` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a copy of the resolution published?
      `the resolution states a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution state a date on which the amendment takes effect?
      `the date the resolution states` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the House's amendment of the secondary legislation I rely on take effect` IS
    `the day an amendment or replacement by resolution takes effect` `the day a copy of the resolution was published` `the date I state`
    WHERE
        `the date I state` MEANS IF `the resolution states a date` THEN JUST `the date the resolution states` ELSE NOTHING

@export By what day must the secondary legislation I rely on be confirmed by an Act (s 121)?
GIVEN `the day it was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the secondary legislation made?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the secondary legislation I rely on be confirmed by an Act` IS
    `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` `the day it was made`

@export Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline (ss 121 to 124)?
GIVEN `the confirmation subpart applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made under an empowering provision listed in Schedule 4 (and, if Schedule 4 limits the matters, does it relate to them)?
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the secondary legislation made?
      `an Act confirms it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act contain a provision to the effect that it confirms the legislation?
      `the day that provision commences` IS A DATE @desc On what day does that provision commence? (any date if there is none)
      `it is still in force on the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the secondary legislation still in force on the deadline?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the secondary legislation I rely on be revoked on the confirmation deadline` IS
    `the legislation is revoked on the deadline` `the confirmation subpart applies to it` (`is unconfirmed legislation` `the confirming commencement I state` `the deadline I work out`) `it is still in force on the deadline`
    WHERE
        `the deadline I work out` MEANS `the deadline for confirmation of legislation made on` `the day it was made`
        `the confirming commencement I state` MEANS IF `an Act confirms it` THEN JUST `the day that provision commences` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under legislation that was not confirmed (s 125)?
GIVEN `the kind of charge` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc What kind of charge is it: a duty, levy or road user charge; an Energy Resources Levy order; a Land Transport Act fee or charge; or a Waste Minimisation Act levy rate?
      `it is made under a provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the legislation made under an empowering provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a refund of a charge imposed under unconfirmed legislation` IS
    `a charge imposed under the unconfirmed legislation is cancelled and, if paid, refunded` `the kind of charge` `when` `it is made under a provision listed in Part 2 of Schedule 4`

§§ `Proceedings against the Parliamentary Counsel Office and its staff (s 146)`

@export May I bring a proceeding against the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO (s 146)?
GIVEN `the defendant is the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you want to sue the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO?
      `the proceeding is for a liability of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding for a liability of the PCO itself?
      `the proceeding is for an act or omission in performing the functions of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for an act or omission in performing, or intending to perform, the functions, duties or powers of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel?
      `the act or omission was in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or omission in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring a proceeding against the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` IS
    `a proceeding may be brought against the person` `the defendant is the Chief Parliamentary Counsel or an employee of the PCO` `the proceeding is for a liability of the PCO` `the proceeding is for an act or omission in performing the functions of the PCO or the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` `the act or omission was in good faith`

§§ `Transition from the earlier law (Schedule 1)`

@export Does section 26 govern when the secondary legislation I rely on, made before the Act, came into force (Schedule 1 clause 5)?
GIVEN `the day the secondary legislation was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the secondary legislation made?
      `the main commencement date` IS A DATE @desc What is the main commencement date of the Legislation Act 2019?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 26 govern when the secondary legislation I rely on, made before the Act, came into force` IS
    `section 26 applies to secondary legislation made on` `the day the secondary legislation was made` `given the main commencement date` `the main commencement date`

